{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"agent_message","text":"The mitigation is submitted and accepted (`stage: mitigation`).\n\n**Root cause:** The `search` deployment's revision 2 added the label `service-route: frontend` to its pod template. The `frontend` Service selects on that label, so it was routing traffic to the search pod (port 8082) as well as the frontend pod (port 5000). About half of requests to `frontend:5000` were refused.\n\n**Fix:** Removed the `service-route` label from the `search` deployment's pod template with a `kubectl patch`. The rollout completed, and `frontend` endpoints now list only `10.244.162.147:5000`.\n\n**Verification:** Before the fix, 530 of 1000 in-cluster requests (100 concurrent) failed to connect. After it, all 1000 returned 200 (p50 ~220ms, p95 ~233ms under that load).\n\nI did not change any other resources. The `rate` service's `RATE_BACKEND_QPS_LIMIT=500` and `RATE_QUEUE_CAPACITY=256` settings were not implicated, so I left them alone."}}
